{
  "_readme": "Which `#tags` in a note sit inside code, and so are not tags at all.\n\nGenerated by scripts/build-tag-conformance.mjs from @codemirror/lang-markdown —\nthe parser the editor itself uses to decide which tags to draw. The Rust has no\nparser and reimplements the rule by hand; this fixture is what holds the two to\nthe same answer.\n\nIt matters because a tag inside code used to head a block, so deleting that tag\ntook the prose underneath it — while the editor, which knew it was code, drew\nno tag there at all and gave the reader no warning.\n\n`at` is a byte offset to the `#`. `code` is the answer both sides must give.",
